// A literal too wide for a 32-bit int. Up to 18 digits it fits a long long and
// takes the `LL` suffix. From 19 digits it may be 2^63 or more, which no long
// long holds: gcc would read the bare digits as a 128-bit constant, so a
// comparison with a word holding the same bits came out false. It is written
// as an unsigned 64-bit constant reinterpreted as long long, the wrap SPEC 2.1
// gives `word` and the LLVM target's i64 already has.
int_wide(string digits) {
  string text = digits + "LL";
  if(len(digits) >= 19) {
    text = "((long long)" + digits + "ULL)";
  }
} return string text;
("9999999999"):("9999999999LL")
("9223372036854775808"):("((long long)9223372036854775808ULL)")
("18446744073709551615"):("((long long)18446744073709551615ULL)")
